      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find the naming too confusing. You have\n- processMessage\n- processMsgInternal\n- processMsgAndPerformTransition\n\nIt\u0027s very unclear where the 3rd one fits. I would suggest renaming like follows :\n\n- processMessage → processMessage\n- processMsgAndPerformTransition → currentStateProcessMessageThenPerformTransitions\n- processMsgInternal → stateProcessMessageRecursively\n\nIt\u0027s not awesome – you\u0027re welcome to have better ideas\n\nAnother alternative would be to remove processMsgInternal and to inline it. You\u0027d have to linearize it so it\u0027s no longer recursive, but that\u0027s really not difficult :\n\n    mSelfMsgAllowed \u003d true;\n    StateInfo consideredState \u003d mStateInfo.get(mCurrentState);\n    while (null !\u003d consideredState) {\n      if (consideredState.state.processMessage(msg)) {\n        log(\"processed\")\n        break;\n      }\n      consideredState \u003d consideredState.parent;\n    }\n    if (null \u003d\u003d consideredState) {\n      log(\"not handled\");\n    }\n    mSelfMsgAllowed \u003d false;\n\nIf you do that, you no longer have the naming problem.",
      "revId": "1d0edb9a4aa31176cecbe525aae8a9f08dc5c963",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
